-- allium: 4
-- Allium v4 standard library. USER-SPACE definitions (not core built-ins): a spec brings them in with
--   use "<path-to>/std.allium"
-- and then uses min/max/clamp/abs/sign directly. This is the extensibility model in action — the core
-- stays small (arithmetic, comparison, if/then/else, given-means, quantifiers, temporal, one rounding
-- primitive); everything else is a contributable library. Each is proven monitorable.
component Std
  given min(a, b) means if a < b then a else b
  given max(a, b) means if a > b then a else b
  given clamp(x, lo, hi) means max(lo, min(x, hi))
  given abs(x) means if x < 0 then 0 - x else x
  given sign(x) means if x < 0 then 0 - 1 else (if x > 0 then 1 else 0)
end
